  "independence": "Manual likelihood recurrence, goal masks, smoothed softmax distributions, outer joint mixture formulas, all raw row domains, full metric/bin formulas, equal-game summaries and gate. Reuses unchanged public combat rules/tactical_scores and original fixed hypothesis helper. Does not invoke GoalOpponentMemory, GoalBeliefs, evaluate_run or study metric helpers for raw-data verification. Rule replay invokes resolve only after forecasts are independently reconstructed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Likelihood weights rank supplied tactical experts; they do not identify a true hidden goal or psychological type.",
    "Single public-route masks make adaptive and equal-goal predictions identical regardless of retained weights; the 28 tied games must not be credited to inference.",
    "Experts can coincide on actions or states and different intentions/controllers can choose the same action, preventing semantic identification.",
    "No latent true-goal ground truth or well-specified generative model is available; weights are discounted bounded engineering evidence, not calibrated Bayesian goal posteriors.",
    "Full intent improvement can coexist with worse movement-occupancy prediction.",
    "Independent goal products assume no learned opponent coordination; fixed joint dependence is preserved.",
    "Familiar scenarios and controller families with fresh seeds are not novel-distribution or external validation.",
    "No gameplay decisions use these predictions; no win-rate, live throughput, or cost-benefit claim follows."
  ],
  "nonblocking_suggestions": [
    "Leak-test mocks at combat bindings alone do not cover every imported alias; current source inspection verifies the present boundary."
